## On Every Session Start

**Always do this first:**
1. Read all files in `docs/mindmaps/` to understand current project state
2. Silently note: what exists, what is in progress, what is next

If you want a spoken/written briefing, run `/orient`.

## Skills Available

### Project Navigation

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `/orient` | Full briefing — what the project is, what's built, what's next |
| `/update_mindmaps` | Regenerate all mind maps from current docs, code, and git history |

### Spec-Driven Development (`sdd_*`)

Run these in order for each feature. Each ends with a human review touchpoint before the next begins.

| Command | Step | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `/sdd_feature_brief <feature-name>` | 1 | What to build — user stories, acceptance criteria, scope |
| `/sdd_tech_design <feature-name>` | 2 | How to build it — design per system layer, offline/sync if applicable |
| `/sdd_api_spec <feature-name>` | 3 | Exact contracts — endpoints, schemas, event payloads |
| `/sdd_impl_plan <feature-name>` | 4 | Individual coding tasks in dependency order |
| `/sdd_test_spec <feature-name>` | 5 | Unit, integration, and end-to-end tests |
| `/sdd_adr <feature-name> <decision-title>` | Any | Capture an architectural decision and its rationale |
| `/sdd_consistency_check <feature-name>` | Any | Read-only cross-check of all pipeline docs + implementation |

Output is saved to `docs/features/<feature-name>/` with numbered files.

Run `/update_mindmaps` at the end of any significant work session to keep context fresh.
